.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH sam-jail-preset 1 2026-11-10 "SAM 0.1.0" "SAM Manual"
.SH NAME
sam\-jail\-preset \- Manage presets
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsam\-jail preset\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage presets
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
sam\-jail\-preset\-list(1)
.TP
sam\-jail\-preset\-show(1)
.TP
sam\-jail\-preset\-apply(1)
Apply a preset to an app (asks for confirmation when it conflicts)
.TP
sam\-jail\-preset\-check(1)
What applying a preset would change for an AppImage without a sandbox (the settings shown now as a PermissionSet on stdin with \-\-current\-stdin). Changes nothing
.TP
sam\-jail\-preset\-save(1)
Save an app\*(Aqs current permissions as a new preset
.TP
sam\-jail\-preset\-delete(1)
.TP
sam\-jail\-preset\-duplicate(1)
.TP
sam\-jail\-preset\-import(1)
.TP
sam\-jail\-preset\-export(1)
.TP
sam\-jail\-preset\-put(1)
Create or replace a user preset from JSON on stdin
.TP
sam\-jail\-preset\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
